w11 patched labwc -- native-toplevel geometry (AGENTS.md route 6)
================================================================

Why this exists
---------------
On the wlr floor (labwc, and the labwc-backed Budgie / Xfce-on-Wayland /
LXQt-on-Wayland sessions) w11's window backend answers an XWayland window's real
rectangle over the X plane (route 5), but a NATIVE Wayland toplevel had no
rectangle at all: zwlr_foreign_toplevel_management_v1 and
ext_foreign_toplevel_list_v1 carry a title and an app id and no geometry, and no
X server has heard of the window. So `wdotool getwindowgeometry` on a native
window answered `0,0 out_w x out_h` -- the whole output.

The lowest reachable rung for the labwc family is route 6: patch the compositor,
ship it as a package. This patch makes labwc publish each view's rectangle.

The runtime contract
--------------------
The patched labwc writes $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/w11-labwc-geometry, rewritten
atomically (temp + rename) on every view map, move/resize, unmap and
title/app_id change (the join key below: a first cut without the title hook
let a foot that renamed itself after map fall back to the floor). One line
per view that carries a foreign-toplevel handle -- exactly the set the
foreign-toplevel protocols advertise -- tab-separated:

    <pid>\t<x>\t<y>\t<w>\t<h>\t<app_id>\t<title>

x/y/w/h are the view's current content rectangle (view->current), the same
rectangle getwindowgeometry prints for an XWayland view on this floor. Tabs,
newlines and carriage returns in app_id/title are replaced with spaces so the
line format is stable; title is the last field.

w11 reads it in hacks/window/backend_wlr.py (WlrBackend._labwc_geometry): when a
native row has no X client to join, its rectangle and pid are folded in by
(app_id, title), the same pair match_xids pairs the X plane on. A key two
windows share is dropped, so a tie keeps the floor rather than guess.

Build (Ubuntu 26.04 "resolute", labwc 0.9.3-1)
----------------------------------------------
    sudo sed -i 's/^Types: deb$/Types: deb deb-src/' \
        /etc/apt/sources.list.d/ubuntu.sources    # or add a deb-src stanza
    sudo apt-get update
    sudo apt-get build-dep -y labwc
    apt-get source labwc                            # labwc-0.9.3
    cd labwc-0.9.3
    mkdir -p debian/patches
    cp .../packaging/labwc/0001-w11-native-toplevel-geometry.patch debian/patches/
    echo 0001-w11-native-toplevel-geometry.patch >> debian/patches/series
    # bump debian/changelog to 0.9.3-1w11.1 (see the stanza in build-deb notes)
    dpkg-buildpackage -b -uc -us
    # -> ../labwc_0.9.3-1w11.1_amd64.deb

The .deb depends only on libwlroots-0.19 (0.19.2-1), which resolute already
ships -- no wlroots rebuild. One package covers all four labwc goldens.

Install / measure
-----------------
    sudo apt-get install -y --allow-downgrades ./labwc_0.9.3-1w11.1_amd64.deb
    systemctl restart greetd     # restart the session so patched labwc runs

Measured on the resolute-labwc golden 2026-09-14: a native foot the compositor
placed at 612,306 696x494 read `0,0 1920x1080` out of wdotool getwindowgeometry
with stock labwc and `612,306 696x494` with this .deb installed.

Upstreaming
-----------
The upstreamable form of the same emit is a foreign-toplevel protocol event
carrying the rectangle (labwc already ships cosmic-workspace; cosmic's
zcosmic_toplevel_handle_v1.geometry is the matching shape). That would make the
row AGENTS.md route 1 in a later Ubuntu, with no runtime file.
